# E0052: call of a function that does not exist

A call must name a function of the program, a class, `print`, or a conversion `i64(...)` or `u8(...)`.

When a function, class, `print` or conversion has a similar name, the error offers it as a guess. The guess may be wrong: the name could be a function that was never written.

## Why

Sisu does not resolve a misspelled function name on its own. A misspelled name, or a function that was never written, would otherwise run some other code or none.

## Broken

```sisu
fn total(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 {
    a + b
}

fn main() {
    print(sum(1, 2))
}
```

## Fixed

```sisu
fn total(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 {
    a + b
}

fn main() {
    print(total(1, 2))
}
```

